# Graph Database Benchmarking Project - Development Explanation

## 1. Project Idea

The purpose of this project was to compare the performance of different graph database platforms using the same graph dataset and identical query workloads.

The main goal was to measure how different databases handle graph operations such as node lookup, relationship traversal, and aggregation queries.

---

## 2. Project Planning

First, I selected a public graph dataset suitable for benchmarking.

Dataset selected:

- cit-HepPh (High Energy Physics Citation Network)

The dataset represents citation relationships between research papers.

For a fair comparison, the same dataset was used in all databases.

---

## 3. Technology Selection

The following graph databases were selected:

- Neo4j
- Memgraph
- ArangoDB
- CognoDB

Python was chosen as the programming language to automate:

- Database connections
- Data loading
- Benchmark execution
- Result processing

